gui or required\nvia cli console or a central management console at\nno additional license /cost.\n51. inbuild diagnostic and policy testing tool in gui for required\ntroubleshooting.\n52. tcp dump utility in command line for advance required\ntroubleshooting\n53. firewall should be able to keep minimum two required\nfirmware version and admin should be able to roll\nback to previous version from gui without\nuploading firmware.\n54. firewall product/products family of oem should have required\nmtcte certification from tec\n55. oem support (tac) presence in india required\n56. escalation matrix for support required\n57. software os family should be having at least one required\ncommon criteria eal4 certificate or equivalent\nindian certification.\nrayalaseemauniversity, kurnool\ne-tender document to rayalaseema university, kurnool\nannexureii\neligibility criteria\n1\nfirm registration certificate from registrar of companies/societies/msme mandatory\n2\ngoods service tax registration mandatory\n3\npan number of the firm/individual mandatory\n4\nit returns for the last three (3) financial years mandatory\nmanufacturer / oem authorization letter needs to be submitted for this specific\n5 tender and also authorizing the bidder to submit the bid for tendering which is\nmandatory\ndeemed as an agreement in between the bidder and oem for the support and\nspares till the warrant period.\nthe bidder should furnished annexure-i providing compliance to the technical\n6\nspecification listed along with relevant brochure, certificate etc.,(compliance mandatory\nreport should be enclosed with duly signed)\nthe bidder should submit/give undertaking in compliance with gfr rule\n7\nmandatory\n144(xi) as per the annexure-iv of this tender document.\nthe bidder should have a cumulative turnover of at least rs.1crore for the last 3\n8\nmandatory\nfinancial years.\nthe bidder should have executed similar nature of work worth of rs. 30 lakh and\n9\nabove during last three financial years for any state or central government mandatory\ninstitutions (must enclosed at least one work order)\nthe bidder should submit/give declaration stating that they are not debarred /\nblacklisted by any state government, central government state govt.\n10\nundertakings/enterprises/organizations and by any other quasi government mandatory\nbodies / organizations in india for non-satisfactory performance, corrupt\nfraudulent or any other unethical business practices during past 5financial years.\nsignature of the bidder with full address,\ncontact number(s) and mail id\n(to be signed by the authorized signatory)\nrayalaseemauniversity, kurnool\ne-tender document to rayalaseema university, kurnool\nannexure-iii\nfinancial bid\nname of the bidder / firm :\ngst number :\nitem: 1 - network\ns. no item unit grand\ngst total\nitem description code qty price total\n(inr) (inr)\n(inr) (inr)\n1 18-port gigabit easy smart\n5 nos\nswitch with 16-port poe\n2 ceiling mount wi-fi 6\n94 nos\naccess point\n3 hardware controller for 01 no\nswitches and access points\n4 10-port gigabit smart\n6 nos\nswitch with 8-port poe\n5 cat 6 cable 10 boxes\n6 6 core single mode fiber 1300 mtrs\ncable\n7 24-port gigabit and 4-port 13 nos\n10ge sfp l2 managed\nswitch with 24-port poe\n8 26-port 10g stackable l3 1 no\nmanaged aggregation\nswitch with 6 25g slots\n9 lc-lc single mode patch 36 nos\ncords\n10 cat6 rj45 utp jack 5 boxes\n11 cat6 utp patch cord 3 10 nos\nmtrs\n12 cat6 utp patch cord 1 mtr 10 nos\n13 9u rack 17 nos\n14 pvc conduit pipe with 2500 mtrs\naccessories\n15 sfpmodulesinglemode1g 12 nos\n16 sfp 10g modules single 24 nos\nmode modules\n17 6 port fiber liu 6 nos\n18 ofc splicing with 100 nos\ntermination box\n19 otdr testing 1 no\n20 hdpe pipe 1300 mtrs\n21 laying of pvc pipe along\n1 no\nwith cat 6 cable\n22 ofccablelaying and\n1 no\ndigging\n23 installation, testing,\n1 no\ncommissioning and\ntraining\nitem: 2 - firewall\ns. no unit price grand\ntotal gst\nitem description qty (inr) total (inr)\n(inr) (inr)\n1 fire wall\n1 no.\nprices inclusive of all taxes should be quoted.\nsignature of the bidder with full address, contact number(s) and mail id\n(to be signed by the authorized signatory)\nannexure-iv\nundertaking incompliance with gfr rule 144(xi)\nto date:\nthe registrar\nrayalaseema university\nkurnool.\ndear sir,\nsub: tender for\nref: tender reference\ni/we, bidder/oem name have read the clause regarding restrictions on procurement from a\nbidder/ oem of a country which shares a land border with india.\ni/we hereby certify that i/we, oem/bidder nameis not from any such country or, if from\nsuch a country, has been registered with the following competent authority:\n1. details of competent authority:\n2. registration certificate ref. no.:\n3. products for which registered:( registration should be valid for the offered product)\ni/we hereby certify that i/we in the event of becoming a successful bidder shall not sub-\ncontract works to any contractor from a country which shares a land border with india unless\nsuch contractor is registered with the competent authority, as per gfr rule 144(xi).\ni/we hereby certify that i/we fulfill all requirements in this regard and eligible to be\nconsidered\nfor oem/bidd\nauthorized signatory:\nname of the authorized person:\ndesignation:\nname of bidder:\nstamp o fbidder:\nnote:\n1. the letter should be submitted on the letter head of the bidder/oem and should be\nsigned by the authorised signatory.\n2. any deviation would lead to summary rejection of bids.\ne-tenderletter\ndate:\nto\nthe registrar\nrayalaseema university, kurnool.\nref: your tender notice no....dated.\n\ni/we have read the contents of the terms and conditions mentioned in your tender\nschedule and its enclosures and agree to abide by the same.\ni/we hereby offer to supply the articles prescribed in the schedule (or such portion\nthereof as you may specify on the acceptance of tender) at the price given.\ni/we agree to hold this offer open for a period of ninety days (90) from the date of\nacceptance of tender and shall be bound by communication of acceptance dispatched\nwithin a period of 15 days from the date of opening of tenders.\ni/we have also examined the requisite specifications of the material to be supplied and\nmy/our offer is to supply the required material in accordance with the requisite\nspecifications.\ni/we have carefully considered all terms and conditions sated in the tender documents\nand particulars regarding settlement of disputes and we have signed the same in token of\nconsciously accepting the same and do hereby state that we accept them without any\nreservations and accordingly.\ni/we quote the rate inclusive of all taxes, duties, transportation, insurance etc.\nthe articles will be ready for delivery within days from the date of receipt of firm\norders.\nyours faithfully\n(signature and stamp of the tenderer, state legal status,\nwhether prop partner, registered firm, company etc.)\ndeclaration\n1. i, son/daughter/wife of\nsri proprietor / director / authorized signatory of\nthe service provider, mentioned above, am competent to sign this declaration and execute\nthis tender document.\n2. i have carefully read and understood all the terms and conditions of the tender and\nundertake to abide by them\n3. i hereby declare that the firm has not been blacklisted by any department /institution in the\nstate government/central government due to any reason\n4. i hereby declare that the firm was not disqualified for any wrong declaration.\n5. the information/documents furnished along with the above application are true and\nauthentic to the best of my knowledge and brief. i/we am/are well aware of the fact that\nfurnishing of any false information/fabricated document would lead to rejection of my tender\nat any stage besides liabilities towards prosecution under appropriate law\nsignature of authorized person\ndate: full name:\nplace: seal:','2026-07-25 03:21:49'),(2,1,'1746602049.pdf','09f8815a-9e94-423c-899c-aeab0c230f8a_1746602049.pdf','tender document\ninstruction to the bidders\nbidders are invited from the reputed and capable organisations /companies/ firms/ oems/ retailers for the\nsupply of 150 high-end desktop computer at iiit pune. relevant documents consisting of the general\ntender document and scope of supply can be downloaded from institute website (www.iiitp.ac.in) or may\nbe downloaded from gem portal http://gem.gov.in. the institute reserves the right to issue tender paper and\nreject any or all of the tenders without assigning any reason thereof. if the last date of opening of tender\ncoincides with a holiday or an unforeseen situation the same will be deferred to the next working day.\naspiring bidders who have not enrolled /registered in gem should enrol/ register before participating through\nthe website https://mkp.gem.gov.in/registration/signup.\nbidders can access tender documents on the gem portal. select the appropriate tender and fill them with all\nrelevant information and submit the completed tender document online on the website http://gem.gov.in as\nper the schedule given in the next page.\nthe bidding shall be conducted under two-packet bidding process on gem portal.\nunder the two-packet bidding process, the bidder shall not quote, disclose or submit its price in the technical\npart (first packet) of its bid or in any other manner, whatsoever, except as part of the financial part (second\npacket) of its bid. in case of any non-compliance in this regard, the bids shall be out-rightly / summarily\nrejected.\nbid must be submitted online through the e-procurement/ e-tendering process as per gem. any bid or\nmodifications to bid received outside the e-procurement system will not be considered.\npage 1 of 21\nterms and conditions of the contract\n1. optional clause: the purchaser reserves the right to increase or decrease the quantity to be ordered up to 25\npercent of bid quantity at the time of placement of